{"id":"icefields-parkway-bike","title":"Icefields Parkway by bike","who":"Classic route · the Canadian Rockies","when":"Mid-June to mid-September","vehicle":"Road or touring bike, 3–5 days","kind":"bike","color":"#0284c7","summary":"About 230 km between Jasper and Lake Louise along the spine of the Rockies: a hundred glaciers, turquoise lakes, Bow Summit at 2,134 m, the Columbia Icefield, bears and goats by the road. Lodges and campgrounds are few and book up early. Jasper was hit by wildfire in July 2024.","sources":[{"label":"Rider Magazine: above the timberline, Canada's Rocky Mountain corridor","url":"https://ridermagazine.com/above-the-timberline-riding-canadas-wild-rocky-mountain-corridor/"},{"label":"10Adventures: cycle Jasper to Banff","url":"https://www.10adventures.com/cycle-jasper-to-banff/"}],"approximate":"Main stops; the line follows Highway 93.","km":239,"bbox":[-118.0825,51.4252,-116.1777,52.8752],"stops":[{"name":"Jasper","place":"Jasper, Alberta","at":[52.8752,-118.0824],"text":"A mountain town recovering from the 2024 wildfire.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Jasper_from_the_Jasper_Tramway_2008.jpg/500px-Jasper_from_the_Jasper_Tramway_2008.jpg","page":"Jasper, Alberta","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jasper_from_the_Jasper_Tramway_2008.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Athabasca Falls","place":"Athabasca Falls","at":[52.6644,-117.8835],"text":"A thundering gorge just off the road.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Athabasca_Falls_-_Jasper.jpg/500px-Athabasca_Falls_-_Jasper.jpg","page":"Athabasca Falls","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Athabasca_Falls_-_Jasper.jpg","credit":"Wikimedia Commons","license":"free licence"}},{"name":"Sunwapta Falls","place":"Sunwapta Falls","at":[52.5323,-117.6446],"text":"Into the wilder southern half.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t